      "topic": "travel",
      "title_zh": "车票在哪儿？",
      "title_en": "Where's the ticket?",
      "paragraphs": [
        ["上", "个", "月", "，", "我", "和", "姐姐", "要", "坐", "火车", "去", "上海", "。", "我们", "到", "了", "火车站", "，", "人", "非常", "多", "。"],
        ["姐姐", "说", "：", "“", "车票", "在", "哪儿", "？", "”", "我", "找", "了", "找", "，", "没有", "找到", "！"],
        ["最后", "，", "我", "在", "包", "里", "找到", "了", "。", "我们", "都", "笑", "了", "。"],
        ["上", "了", "火车", "，", "姐姐", "说", "：", "“", "关上", "门", "吧", "，", "有", "风", "。", "”"],
        ["我们", "坐", "了", "五", "个", "小时", "，", "到", "了", "上海", "。"]
      ],
      "translations": [
        "Last month my older sister and I were taking the train to Shanghai. When we got to the station it was packed.",
        "My sister said: “Where are the tickets?” I looked and looked, but couldn't find them!",
        "In the end I found them in my bag. We both laughed.",
        "Once we were on the train, my sister said: “Shut the door — there’s a draught.”",
        "Five hours later we arrived in Shanghai."
      ],
      "names": ["上海"],
      "new_words": ["火车站", "车票", "关上"],
      "glossary": [
        { "word": "火车站", "english": "train station" },
        { "word": "车票", "english": "ticket (train or bus)" },
        { "word": "关上", "english": "to close; to shut" },
        { "word": "上海", "english": "Shanghai" }
      ]
    }
